	skos:definition	"This industry subgroup includes companies that invest in a leveraged buyout asset class of private equity financial sponsors. A leveraged buyout occurs when a financial sponsor acquires a controlling interest in a company's equity and a significant percentage of the purchase price is financed through leverage."@en ;
