	skos:definition	"This industry includes real estate investment trusts (REITs). REITS own and develop income-producing real estate and real estate mortgages. Sectors include office, retail, housing, healthcare, hotel, industrial, self-storage and specialty. To be considered a REIT, a company must have most of its assets and income tied to real estate and must distribute at least 90% of it taxable income as dividends to shareholders."@en ;
