	skos:definition	"This industry subgroup includes companies that produce reconstructive and spinal devices that are used to repair lost joint function (orthopedic devices), spinal conditions (spinal implants), and damaged bones and tissue (bone cement and fixation devices such as screws, pins, plates, etc.). Products include hip and knee implants, spinal plates and screws, orthobiologics, bone cement and dental devices."@en ;
	tempo:validFrom	"2014-08-08"^^xsd:date ;
	tempo:validTill	"2020-10-03"^^xsd:date .

